From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:15:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: make an off-region block read fail attributably

Level#getBlockStateIfLoaded dereferences getCurrentWorldData() with no null
check, so a block read from a thread that owns no region of that world ends in
an NPE naming captureTreeGeneration - a field with nothing to do with the
problem - instead of the platform's own ownership error with thread context,
world, position and a stack trace.

Ask the platform to report it. ensureTickThread either throws that error, or (if
the thread does own the position but somehow has no world data) does not, and
the caller falls through to the original NPE. The outcome is unchanged either
way: the read already failed and still fails.

Only this method, the one path with measured evidence - 26 occurrences in one
soak run, all from CraftWorld#rayTraceBlocks off-region.

Kill switch: -Dlophinya.compat.regionReadDiagnostics=false

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java
index ca92bb3a8b739c0da3f48a2dd16c5fb4fa7e8453..97465a24485f3636dc34c74840b2374ebe78dc66 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/Level.java
@@ -1012,6 +1012,11 @@ public abstract class Level implements LevelAccessor, AutoCloseable, ca.spottedl
     @Override
     @Nullable
     public final BlockState getBlockStateIfLoaded(BlockPos pos) {
+        // Lophinya start - attribute the off-region read instead of letting it NPE on a field name
+        if (fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaRegionReadDiagnostics.ENABLED && this.getCurrentWorldData() == null) {
+            fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaRegionReadDiagnostics.reportMissingWorldData(this, pos);
+        }
+        // Lophinya end
         // CraftBukkit start - tree generation
         if (this.getCurrentWorldData().captureTreeGeneration) { // Folia - region threading
             CraftBlockState previous = this.getCurrentWorldData().capturedBlockStates.get(pos); // Folia - region threading
